    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T08:43:50Z",
    "body": "Issue sweep: partly done on `upstream/main`, so this issue stays open.\n\nDone on `upstream/main`:\n- PR #2797 (`02d08c9bd`, merge commit `c4ac3ce6d`) moved the solidcore pin to `2016386442dfee3b2a0c3a1bfdd4017c5254dac8`.\n- `Milling-test.step` and `Milling-test-inch.step` now pass with `agree` in `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement/rows.rs` (`step_milling_test` and `step_milling_test_inch`).\n\nStill open:\n- `docs/decisions/917-kernel-pcurves.md` does not name the root cause of finding 1. The upstream fix is solidcore commit `ae5f59c18`, which retired `face_tight_box_searches_trim`.\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs` (`StepSolid::measure`) and `crates/kernel/tests/solidcraft_import.rs` still keep the old warning comment about `#939`.\n- Pin `2016386442` does not fix finding 2 (`to_kernel_body` stale cached topology). `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs` still calls `brep.refresh_cached_topology()`.\n- Pin `2016386442` does not fix finding 3 (no cancel hook in `solidcore_step::topology::read_solids` or `read_solids_with`).\n- Upstream issues `tangency-labs/solidcore#3256` and `tangency-labs/solidcore#3257` stay open.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
